/.well-known/assetlinks.json  /.well-known/assetlinks.json  200
/privacy /privacy.html 200
# Non-web paths: source, tests, build tooling and schema live in the repo but
# have no business being fetched from the CDN. `!` forces the rule to win over
# the real file. Tidiness, not secrecy — the repository is public, so nothing
# here is hidden by this.
#
# These are inert under the current topology: the publish directory is
# apps/web/dist, which contains none of these paths. They are KEPT because
# reverting the cutover republishes the repo root, and at that moment they are
# load-bearing again. Deleting them would make the rollback quietly worse than
# the thing it rolls back to.
/checks/*            /index.html  404!
/native/*            /index.html  404!
/design/*            /index.html  404!
/netlify/functions/_lib/*  /index.html  404!
/*.sql               /index.html  404!
/*.md                /index.html  404!
/readme.txt          /index.html  404!
/package.json        /index.html  404!
/package-lock.json   /index.html  404!
# React monorepo source. `publish = "."` serves the whole tree, so without
# these the TypeScript sources and node_modules would be fetchable while the
# migration is in flight. The BUILT apps are published from their own dist/,
# not from here.
/packages/*          /index.html  404!
/apps/*              /index.html  404!
/node_modules/*      /index.html  404!
/pnpm-workspace.yaml /index.html  404!
/pnpm-lock.yaml      /index.html  404!
/tsconfig*.json      /index.html  404!

# The athlete SPA fallback. It is deliberately last: every rule above must beat
# it, and Netlify evaluates this file top-down.
#
# The coach app is NOT handled here. Its own fallback lives in netlify.toml,
# because netlify.toml redirects are evaluated BEFORE this file — that ordering
# is the only thing that stops the rule below answering /coach/ deep links with
# the athlete shell. Real files (/coach/index.html, /coach/assets/*) are served
# ahead of both.
/* /index.html 200
